<BES xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="BES.xsd">
  <Fixlet>
    <Title>Troubleshooting - RES ONE Workspace Environment Validation - Windows</Title>
    <Description><![CDATA[
<DIV id=fixletMessage2 class=FixletMessage>
	<DIV id=paramFixletDescription>
		<P>Use this Fixlet will utilize all of the information provided in the RES ONE Workspace Deployment Wizard in a simulation mode -- it will test each parameter individually and make sure that they work in the environment. This is a prerequisite to database deployment.</P>
		<p>
			This works by outputting an exit code which can be translate to a specific error. You can review the exit codes below otherwise we have made the results available in plain english on the  <?relevance link "RES Deployment Health Check Dashboard" of wizards whose (dashboard id of it = "RESHealthCheck.ojo") of site of current fixlet?>.
		</p>
		<P>
			This fixlet will <b>only be applicable against the BigFix Root Server </b> and only if it has SQL Command Line Tools and at least Powershell 2.0 installed. The environment validation will take place using the Root Server as a launching point.
		</P>
		<h5>Exit codes for this fixlet</h5>
		<p>
			<ul>
				<li>10 : SQL Server Not Found</li>
				<li>20 : SQL Authentication Error</li>
				<li>30 : Missing Create Database Permissions in SQL</li>
				<li>40 : Missing Create Table Permissions in the Database</li>
				<li>50 : Invalid NetBIOS Prefix for the BigFix Connector Group</li>
				<li>60 : Invalid Group Name for the BigFix Connector Group</li>
				<li>70 : BigFix Server Missing from the BigFix Connector Group</li>
				<li>80 : Service Account has an incorrect NetBIOS Domain Prefix</li>
				<li>90 : Could not verify the Service Account Credentials</li>
			</ul>
		</p>
	</DIV>
	<DIV id=plainOrdinaryFixletDescription>Failed to load parameterized fixlet.</div>
</div>

<script>
    loaded = false;

	function loadGlobalization() {
		var globalization = EvaluateRelevance('(messages of it) of fixlets whose ( name of it = "Parameterized Fixlet Library") of all bes sites whose (name of it = "BES Support")');
		var regex = /\s*<DIV id=globalizationMessageDiv  style="display:none;">([\x00-\x7F]+)\s*<\/Div>/i;
		var matches = regex.exec(globalization);
		var globalizationSanitized = matches[1].replace(/<br>/gi, "");
		return globalizationSanitized;
	}

	function loadUtils() {
		return EvaluateRelevance('unique value of values of mime fields whose (name of it = "vrt_utils.js") of fixlets whose ( name of it = "Parameterized Fixlet Library") of all bes sites whose (name of it = "BES Support")');
	}

    function loadScript(url, callback) {
		var head = document.getElementsByTagName("head")[0];
		var script = document.createElement("script");
		script.type = "text/javascript";
		script.text = loadUtils() + loadGlobalization();
        script.onreadystatechange = callback;
        script.onload = callback;

        head.appendChild(script);
    }

    function scriptLoaded() {
        if (!loaded) {
            var paramFixletDescription = document.getElementById('paramFixletDescription');
            var plainOrdinaryFixletDescription = document.getElementById('plainOrdinaryFixletDescription');

            if (typeof FixletUtils !== 'undefined') {
                loaded = true;
                paramFixletDescription.style.display = "block";
                plainOrdinaryFixletDescription.style.display = "none";

                FixletUtils.initFixletRender();
            } else {
                paramFixletDescription.style.display = "none";
                plainOrdinaryFixletDescription.style.display = "block";
            }
        }
    }

    loadScript("vrt_fixletUtils.js", scriptLoaded);
</script>
]]></Description>
    <Relevance>exists main gather service</Relevance>
